# Agent judgment

## Clarify before workarounds

If a request hits a platform, API, or tooling constraint the user may not know about, **stop and ask** before implementing. Do not silently add dual paths or compatibility shims.

## Minimal scope

Change only what the task needs. Match existing kit patterns (action utils, prompt parts, worker routes). Do not add features, configs, or abstractions for unrequested cases.

## Clean up dead code

When replacing a path (e.g. chat → command bar), delete unused call sites in the same change. Do not leave parallel stacks “just in case.”

## Shop before house

For new capabilities, prefer maintained packages (`@tldraw/mermaid`, Vercel AI SDK Bedrock provider) over custom layout or provider plumbing.
